QDesktopWidget tests
====================

dwtest prints the screens QDesktopWidget reports and checks how they
follow RandR changes: with RandR 1.5 the screens are the RandR monitors
(XRRGetMonitors), the primary monitor first, the others left to right
and then top to bottom; they are re-read on RandR events and on the
root window's ConfigureNotify (sent by "xrandr --setmonitor"), and
resized()/workAreaResized() are emitted when they change, also if the
root window keeps its size. Not part of the normal build.

    tests/desktopwidget/build.sh      # in tests/desktopwidget/build
    tests/desktopwidget/run.sh        # starts Xephyr :89, runs "check"

    dwtest print                      # on any display: read only
    dwtest watch [secs]               # print every change

"dwtest check" runs xrandr --setmonitor/--delmonitor/-s on its display:
never run it on a real display (run.sh refuses $DISPLAY).
